    (v_test, 2, $q$NON_VERBAL$q$, NULL, 8, $q$Odd one out$q$, $q$Symmetry$q$, $q$odd one out$q$, $q$Which figure is the odd one out?$q$, $q$none$q$, NULL, $q$svg$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><polygon points="16,16 64,16 64,38 34,64 16,64" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><polygon points="40,12 22,34 30,34 30,66 50,66 50,34 58,34" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><polygon points="40,12 64,40 40,68 16,40" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><polygon points="20,20 20,50 40,64 60,50 60,20" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/></svg>$q$, $q$<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 80" width="80" height="80"><polygon points="28,14 14,40 28,66 52,66 66,40 52,14" fill="#9ca3af" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="2"/></svg>$q$, $q$A$q$, $q$Four shapes have a vertical line of symmetry (their left and right halves match). The odd one out has no line of symmetry.$q$),
